import Mathlib

-- Declarations for this item will be appended below by the statement pipeline.

universe u

section

variable {F : Type u} [Group F] [IsFreeGroup F] {m N : ℕ}

/-- Proposition 1-6-6: if `N > 1` and the ordered product `u₁^N ⋯ u_m^N` is trivial in a free
group, then the subgroup generated by `u₁, …, u_m` has rank at most `m / 2`. -/
-- Layer triage:
-- `source-facing`: a finite ordered family `u : Fin m → F` in a free group with the relation
-- `u₁^N ⋯ u_m^N = 1`.
-- `core/canonical`: the generated subgroup `Subgroup.closure (Set.range u)` and its invariant
-- `Group.rank`.
-- `bridge/view`: the textbook word `u₁^N ⋯ u_m^N` is encoded canonically by the ordered list
-- `List.ofFn fun i ↦ u i ^ N`.
-- Domain sampling:
-- 1. `Subgroup.closure (Set.range u)` is the chapter's canonical owner for the subgroup generated
--    by a finite tuple.
-- 2. `Group.rank` is mathlib's canonical owner for the minimum size of a generating set of a
--    finitely generated group.
-- 3. `Subgroup.rank_closure_finset_le_card` shows that rank bounds for finitely generated
--    subgroups are stated on the closure owner rather than by introducing a separate free-basis
--    package.
-- 4. `Matrix.rank_le_half_width_of_vanishing_qfold_column_products` from Lemma `1-6-5` is the
--    chapter's owner-level matrix-rank inequality behind this proposition.
-- Primitive vs. derived:
-- the primitive source data are the tuple `u`, the exponent `N`, and the single relation among
-- the `N`th powers; the generated subgroup and its rank are the canonical derived owner-level
-- objects. No extra wrapper for the subgroup basis is introduced here.
-- Proof sketch: associate to the relation `u₁^N ⋯ u_m^N = 1` the Fox-derivative matrix used in the
-- chapter proof. Lemma `1-6-5` bounds the rank of that matrix by `m / 2`, and the standard
-- Jacobian argument identifies this matrix rank with the rank of the subgroup generated by the
-- `u_i`.
theorem rank_closure_range_le_half_of_prod_powers_eq_one
    (u : Fin m → F) (hN : 1 < N)
    (hprod : (List.ofFn (fun i ↦ u i ^ N)).prod = 1) :
    Group.rank (Subgroup.closure (Set.range u)) ≤ m / 2 := sorry

end
